# Generated test suite — review before committing

SpecGuard generated these tests from `{{ spec_name }}` on {{ generated_at }}.
They are a **draft**, not a finished suite.

## Before you trust any of this

1. Read every test marked `# REVIEW:`. Those are cases where SpecGuard had to
   invent data the spec didn't provide (usually a resource id), or where a model
   proposed the case. They will fail against a real API until you fix them.
2. Run the suite and see what fails:

   ```bash
   SPECGUARD_BASE_URL=https://api.staging.example.com pytest {{ out_dir }}
   ```

3. Move the cases you want to keep into your real suite. Anything left here is
   overwritten the next time you run `specguard generate`.

`conftest.py` and `schemas.py` are scaffolded **once** and never overwritten —
they are yours to edit.

## What was generated

| Kind | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `happy` | The documented success path |
| `validation` | A required field missing, or sent with the wrong type |
| `boundary` | Declared min/max probed at the edge and one step past it |
| `auth` | The same request with no credentials |
| `llm_extra` | Proposed by a model from a field's prose description |

Run one kind at a time with `pytest -m happy`.
